{
  "id": "level-shifter-bss138",
  "name": "4-channel bidirectional logic level shifter (BSS138)",
  "category": "module",
  "description": "Safely connects 5 V signals to 3.3 V pins (and back), e.g. HC-SR04 ECHO to an ESP32 or I2C between 3.3 V and 5 V devices.",
  "datasheet": "https://cdn.sparkfun.com/datasheets/BreakoutBoards/Logic_Level_Bidirectional.pdf",
  "sources": [
    "https://learn.sparkfun.com/tutorials/bi-directional-logic-level-converter-hookup-guide",
    "https://www.sparkfun.com/products/12009",
    "https://www.nxp.com/docs/en/application-note/AN10441.pdf"
  ],
  "confidence": "verified",
  "notes": [
    "Connect HV to the 5 V supply, LV to the 3.3 V supply and GND to the common ground. Both references are required for it to work.",
    "Each channel is one BSS138 MOSFET with 10 kOhm pull-ups to LV and HV (NXP AN10441 circuit). HVn follows HV, LVn follows LV.",
    "Good up to a few hundred kHz (I2C, UART, servo PWM, HC-SR04). Too slow for fast SPI or WS2812 data; use a 74AHCT125 for those.",
    "Pins are open-drain with pull-ups, so two pull-ups add in parallel with any on the I2C board.",
    "SparkFun layout shown: HV side pins HV1, HV2, HV, GND, HV3, HV4 and LV side LV1, LV2, LV, GND, LV3, LV4. Generic boards use the same names but sometimes another order."
  ],
